{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLNMML1SMtRHNawVpHdJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the wrong `apart` result. `bug.apart(t)` now returns `-a*t + a/2 - a/(2*(2*t - 1))` instead of `-a*t`.\n\n**Cause:** `Poly.div` switches to a field, divides, then converts the quotient and remainder back to a ring. For a domain like `ZZ[a]`, that conversion in `PolynomialRing.from_FractionField` (`sympy/polys/domains/polynomialring.py`) did integer division of the numerator by a constant denominator. So `a/2` was silently truncated to `0`, and the remainder `a/2` disappeared.\n\n**Fix:** The conversion now uses `numer.exquo(denom)`. If the division isn't exact, it returns `None`, so `Poly.div` keeps the field result.\n\nI ran `test_partfrac.py`, `test_polytools.py`, `test_polyclasses.py` and `test_constructor.py` in `sympy/polys/tests`. Four tests fail there, including `test_noncommutative_pseudomultivariate` and `test_poly_matching_consistency`. The same tests fail without my change. I didn't run the rest of the `sympy/polys` suite. A full run timed out."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378,"cache_read_input_tokens":31748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378},"output_tokens":407,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"09fc0211-803a-42be-aca0-48da9dd03f3e","uuid":"9f45c33c-419e-45f7-b53f-d94522f86803","timestamp":"2026-11-23T18:55:40.516Z","request_id":"req_011ChLNMMB5WSgm8TztBjhDs"}
